V.No. Mahopadhyay Shri Vinayvijayji attained the lotus feet of the Lord while writing \\\\\\\"Shri Shripal Raas\\\\\\\" during his Chaturmas at Rander in 1638. On his indication \\\\\\\"Shri Shripal Raas\\\\\\\" was completed here by Mahopadhyay Shri Yashovijayji.\\\"}]\\n3e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"24\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Other Temples: Presently there are 5 temples in Rander, here the temple of Lord Neminath is very ancient.\\\"}]\\n3f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"25\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Directions: Rander is situated on the banks of a river, 16 km from Surat. The nearest railway station is Surat. Buses and private vehicles are available from Surat to Rander. There is a sub-shelter and dharamshala in Rander.\\\"}]\\n40:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"26\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Scripture: Vighnahara Parshvanath is mentioned in \\\\\\\"Shri Suryapur Chaitya Paripati\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"108 Naam Garbhit Shri Parshvanath Stavan\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"365 Shri Parshvajin Nammala\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Shri Parshvanath Nammala\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Teerthamala\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Surat Chaitya Paripati\\\\\\\" etc. The main temple of Vighnahara Parshvanath is in Rander. There is a temple of Vighnahara Parshvanath near Mandsaur and also at Devgarh in Udaipur. In Valkeshwar, Babeshwar (Babu Kat Temple) in Mumbai, there is an idol in beautiful parikar with Ashtamangal, Navagraha and ten Digpals. There is an attractive idol of Vighnahara Parshvanath in Antriksha Tirtha and many other temples.\\\"}]\\n41:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"27\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Chant Mantra: \\\\\\\"Om Hree Arham Shri Vighnahara Parshvanathaya Namah\\\\\\\"\\\"}]\\n42:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"28\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Trust: Shri Vighnahara Parshvanath Shwetamba\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"r Jain Tirtha, Shri Adi-Neminath Jain Derasar Pedhi, Uttamram Street, Nisha Falia, Post: Rander, Surat - 395005, Gujarat, India. Phone: 0261-2760149, Mobile: 9925198118.\\\"}]\\n\"])</script></body></html>","rscD